{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Which I did not command him to speak.</b> But I did command his fellow." "<b>And that which speaks in the name of other elohim.</b> Even if he matched the halakhah to forbid the forbidden and to permit the permitted (Sanhedrin 9)." "<b>And shall die.</b> By strangulation. Three — their death is by human hands: the one who prophesies what he did not hear, and what was not said to him but was said to his fellow, and the one who prophesies in the name of idolatry. But the one who suppresses his prophecy, and the one who transgresses the words of a prophet, and the one who transgresses his own words — their death is by the hand of Heaven, as it is said (verse 19) ״אָנֹכִי אֶדְרֹשׁ מֵעִמּוֹ״ (Sanhedrin 9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:38.997986515Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}